Potential biases
- Since committee heads represent the findings of a committee, they will appear vocal and active masking the participation of other committee members in the reasearch
- Majority/Minority whips also speak frequently as part of procedure. It should be important to separate their contributions as whip vs as house member contributing to a discussion
- Hansard is reliable but can be very wordy hence noisy. Important to sift out important things without losing context of topic of discussion and what responses
- Committee meetings are useful tools to see minutes of commitee meetings but these aren't publicly available. Only the final report is tabled.
- Some members who belong to committee feel they have participated sufficiently by contributing in committee meetings leading to silence in the house discussions.
- Real parliament work happens in committees
- Office of Auditor-General report great for NG-CDF and other oversight info, but parliament.go.ke tends to be late to discuss the reports. Prefer using https://www.oagkenya.go.ke/national-government-audit-reports/ for timely OAG reports
